.nh
.TH "PB-POLICY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-policy - Read, test and change the workspace access policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb policy [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
The workspace policy is one file that says who may reach which machines,
previews and tunnels, and how. Read it with get, check a draft with test, see
what a change would do with set --dry-run, save it with set, explain any
decision with explain, and go back to an earlier version with restore. Every
save that changes anyone's access shows the changes and asks for confirmation.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for policy


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-explain(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-get(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-restore(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-schema(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-set(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-test(1)\fP, \fBpb-policy-versions(1)\fP
